# Architecture Candidates & Experiments

Spec: ArchitectureCandidates
Purpose:
  Manage external/internal architecture proposals before adoption.

Lifecycle:
  CANDIDATE → EXPERIMENT → EVIDENCE → ADOPT / REJECT / SUPERSEDE

@architecture.candidate.A<id>
  source:       <external | internal>
  hypothesis:   <pattern description>
  project_fit:  <0-100%>
  risks:        [<risk list>]
  recommended_scope: <domain or component>
  status:       <CANDIDATE | EXPERIMENT | EVALUATING | ADOPTED | REJECTED>

@experiment.E<id>
  candidate:    @architecture.candidate.A<id>
  hypothesis:   <testable claim>
  scope:        <sandbox or limited domain>
  success_criteria:
    - <metric> <operator> <value>
  failure_criteria:
    - <metric> <operator> <value>
  status:       <RUNNING | COMPLETED | ABANDONED>

Adaptation Decisions:
  ADOPT:    external pattern fits project as-is
  ADAPT:    external pattern modified for project constraints
  REJECT:   external pattern unsuitable
  SUPERSEDE: existing rule replaced by new pattern

Navigation:
  Parent: @INDEX.sdd
  ExternalStudy: @../references/sdd/living-specs-best-practices.sdd

State: +
